{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You're here because your kidney function has worsened quickly. Your creatinine was 1.1 last time, but now it's 5.0. Do you have any symptoms like fatigue or swelling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No swelling, and I feel okay. I’ve been eating well. I did have some rib pain, but I’m only taking Tylenol and oxycodone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good, no vomiting or diarrhea. Your urine output seems normal too. Given your multiple myeloma, this kidney issue is likely due to 'cast nephropathy'—a buildup of proteins from the cancer affecting your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s because of the myeloma? I’ve had rising IgA and lambda chains lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your free lambda was 942 last week—very high. That’s likely overwhelming your kidneys. We’ll start treatment right away to reduce the protein load."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What kind of treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start chemotherapy—CyBorD: cyclophosphamide, bortezomib, and dexamethasone. We’ll also give you plasmapheresis to filter the harmful proteins from your blood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Plasmapheresis? How does that work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll place a special line in your neck to remove your blood, filter out the abnormal proteins, and return the cleaned blood. It’s like dialysis but targets the myeloma proteins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. And the chemo—same as before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-08-01 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, CyBorD. You’ve had it before. We’re restarting it because your myeloma is progressing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-08-02 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a kidney ultrasound this morning. Good news—it shows no blockage or stones. Both kidneys are normal in size and appearance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-08-02 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing’s physically wrong with them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-08-02 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No obstruction. The damage is internal, from the protein buildup. That’s why chemo and plasmapheresis are key."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-08-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we’ll place the pheresis line in your right neck vein. It’ll be used for plasmapheresis over the next few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-08-04 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-08-04 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use local numbing and a little sedation. You’ll feel pressure but not sharp pain. The team will monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-08-04 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The line was placed successfully. You’ll start plasmapheresis now. We’ll do three sessions over the next few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-08-04 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How will I feel during it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-08-04 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most people feel fine. Some get lightheaded or chilled. We’ll give fluids and monitor your blood pressure closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-08-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your first plasmapheresis went well. We removed a lot of abnormal protein. Your creatinine is still high at 4.8, but we expect gradual improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-08-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any side effects from the chemo?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-08-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching for neuropathy, especially since you already have some. Bortezomib can worsen it. Let us know if your feet feel more numb or painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-08-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-08-06 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has been high—up to 170s. We’re increasing your carvedilol and diltiazem. We may add another medication if it doesn’t settle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-08-06 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been stressed. Could that be why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-08-06 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stress can play a role, but with myeloma and kidney issues, BP control is important. We’ll get it under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-08-07 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Second plasmapheresis done. Your creatinine is down to 3.9. That’s a good sign your kidneys are starting to recover."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-08-07 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! Any update on my blood sugar? I’m on more steroids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-08-07 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your sugars are higher. We’ve increased your Lantus to 46 units at night. You’ll need close monitoring after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-08-07 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll follow up with endocrinology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-08-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we’re giving your second dose of bortezomib through the central line. How are you feeling overall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-08-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired, but okay. My mouth feels dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-08-08 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. We’ll keep you hydrated. Also, you’re still on vancomycin for C. diff. You’ve completed the intensive phase and are now on a taper."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-08-08 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll keep taking it at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-08-08 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, daily at first, then every other day, then every third day. It’s to prevent another flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-08-09 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your third plasmapheresis is scheduled. Also, your left leg has some swelling. We did an ultrasound to check for a clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-08-09 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-08-09 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We had to rule it out. The ultrasound showed no DVT—good news. The swelling may be from inactivity or mild fluid retention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-08-09 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Plasmapheresis complete. Your creatinine is now 3.1. Kidney function is steadily improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-08-09 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a big drop!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-08-09 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and your free lambda is coming down too. The treatment is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-08-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure is better—150s now. We added doxazosin last night, and it’s helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-08-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any side effects I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-08-10 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Dizziness when standing up. Take it at bedtime, and rise slowly. It’s to help relax your blood vessels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-08-10 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-08-10 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs show creatinine down to 2.6. Nephrology agrees you don’t need dialysis. You’re making good progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2176-08-10 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2176-08-10 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow, if all goes well. We’ll remove the pheresis line in the morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2176-08-10 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2176-08-10 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home on the same chemo regimen, with vancomycin taper, insulin at 46 units, and the new doxazosin for blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2176-08-10 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the insulin—what if my sugar drops?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2176-08-10 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Check your morning blood sugar. If it’s below 100, cut the Lantus dose in half—down to 23 units—until you see endocrinology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2176-08-10 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll write that down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2176-08-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We removed the line—no issues. Your vitals are stable, and labs confirm continued improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2176-08-11 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m ready to go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2176-08-11 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll follow up with oncology, nephrology, and endocrinology. Keep taking all meds as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2176-08-11 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2176-08-11 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your team or go to the ER if you have trouble urinating, severe fatigue, shortness of breath, or very low blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2176-08-11 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2176-08-11 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Keep up the good work, and we’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2176-08-11 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before discharge. Your physical exam is stable—clear lungs, normal heart, no swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2176-08-11 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to get home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2176-08-11 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have your wife pick you up. Make sure she reviews the discharge instructions with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2176-08-11 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "She’s on her way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2176-08-11 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge papers are ready. You’re cleared to go home. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2176-08-11 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2176-08-11 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay in touch with your care team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2176-08-11 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in one last time. Any questions before you leave?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2176-08-11 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got it all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2176-08-11 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2176-08-11 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ride is here. Don’t forget your prescriptions and instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2176-08-11 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got them. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2176-08-11 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final sign-out complete. You’re officially discharged. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad you’re going home feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Me too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stay safe and call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final chart note completed. Discharge confirmed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2176-08-11 18:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "All set. Heading home now."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-08-01 21:18:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-08-11 18:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for acute kidney injury with a creatinine rise from 1.1 to 5.0, attributed to cast nephropathy secondary to relapsed multiple myeloma. He was started on CyBorD chemotherapy and underwent three sessions of plasmapheresis, which led to improvement in renal function, with creatinine decreasing to 2.6 at discharge. He received continuous IV fluids and had a temporary pheresis line placed. His blood pressure was managed with uptitration of carvedilol and diltiazem and addition of doxazosin. Insulin was increased to 46 units of Lantus due to steroid-induced hyperglycemia. Oral vancomycin was continued on a taper for recurrent C. diff. He remained stable, avoided dialysis, and was discharged home with follow-up in oncology, nephrology, and endocrinology.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Multiple myeloma in relapse",
      "Enterocolitis due to Clostridium difficile",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with diabetic neuropathy, unspecified",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease with stage 1 through stage 4 chronic kidney disease, or unspecified chronic kidney disease",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult) (pediatric)",
      "Sickle-cell trait",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of prostate",
      "Chronic viral hepatitis B without delta-agent",
      "Anemia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
